{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964515-ascension","id":964515,"title":"Ascension","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-06T14:15:28-07:00","id":964515,"title":"Ascension","content":"Out of curiosity has anyone ever run a game where their Player Characters actually achieved Ascension?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T19:32:04-07:00","id":964721,"title":"","content":"That would be an exceedingly boring game honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T19:41:05-07:00","id":964726,"title":"","content":"Why do you say that? Sounds like you lack imagination if you can't see a game where a character works to reach Ascension and eventually succeeds a boring game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T19:42:48-07:00","id":964728,"title":"","content":"Yeah but then what? They fly up into the heavens as a bolt of light? Good job, make a new character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T19:46:24-07:00","id":964729,"title":"","content":"Yeah you would retire the character or more likely it would happen at the end of the campaign but it is something you can make a story of and that is what I was wanting to know. What stories people have done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T21:31:31-07:00","id":964770,"title":"","content":"What's wrong with rolling a new character? I've come up with dozens of possible characters since I got into Mage that I would give my right arm to run (had I anyone to run a game with). Sometimes you just want to try a different approach to magic out, you know? Especially with a Focus system as open-ended as Mage's.<br /> <br /> On another note, if you've developed a character enough that they achieve true enlightenment, what more can you do with them? You've reached the end of their character arc, so to speak, and done so in the most thorough way possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T03:55:13-07:00","id":964884,"title":"","content":"Well, it's less boring than a game in which Werewolfs encounter the Apocalypse. What happens after that? Nothing. Can I make a new character? No, everything is gone.<br /> Honestly, it would be a game of abject failure.<br /> <br /> Back to the topic, Ascension is one of those things that a lot of mages talk about, but few actually understand. It's the mysterious ideal that always lies just out of reach. What's more interesting to me would be a game about mages who constantly try to achieve Ascension but always find something is holding them back.<br /> A powerful hermetic may think that all they need is to max out their Arete, but doing so only cements them in the folds of the reality they control.<br /> An Akashic may think achieving ascension requires perfecting their mind and may work tirelessly to do this by countless journeys into the astral realm, increased isolation to avoid distraction, and the gradual removal of any and all material things, until the only thing holding them back is their determination to ascend.<br /> An Etherite may think to ascend is to build the most perfect machine, a verbena may think it's to bring themselves back to their primordial roots, you get the idea.<br /> <br /> The idea would be to have the focus be on their dogged determination, and how said determination is the biggest barrier to achieving their goal.<br /> <br /> As an aside, one of the last books released for mage after the reckoning subplot was the Ascension storyline. It gave details on the possibilities the mage universe had for a definitive end and ranged from mass ascension, to Nephandi victory as the world descends into oblivion. So if you wanted to see a few &quot;final&quot; story lines, that would be a good place to start.<br /> <br /> That being said, the books been decanonised since writing the revised convention books. Turns out giving a final end to the world isn't very good for selling books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-07-2016, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T08:42:37-07:00","id":964987,"title":"","content":"That is very true and I like a game where a mage is constantly improving themselves. It's part of why Questing is my favorite essence as it isn't the end goal that's important but the journey of how you get there. One of the reasons that I mage this thread is I was curious how others have handled character Ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:27:18-07:00","id":965181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964515-ascension?p=964726#post964726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you say that? Sounds like you lack imagination if you can't see a game where a character works to reach Ascension and eventually succeeds a boring game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on the opening, the premise seemed to me &quot;Your characters have ACHIEVED Ascension. What do you do now?&quot; Which.... just seems rather dull.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:49:11-07:00","id":965198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964515-ascension?p=965181#post965181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Based on the opening, the premise seemed to me &quot;Your characters have ACHIEVED Ascension. What do you do now?&quot; Which.... just seems rather dull.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my bad for the wording. I was just wanting to hear what stories if any people have played where characters have achieved it. How people have handled it and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T01:04:30-07:00","id":966672,"title":"","content":"Actually, for a one shot session, it could be interesting. In my chronicle, characters are still noobs (3 year old Mages) and I thought at doing an End of Times Scenario with Mages close to reaching Ascension just to show some other aspects of the game that they will not encounter anytime soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T09:13:42-07:00","id":1302240,"title":"","content":"I am disappointed in many of you in this thread. Many of you are stating that a game like that would be boring and implying there would be no point. Don't you know what a story is? It's all in how you tell it. Use some imagination. Just because you think it's boring doesn't mean it's a dead end game. My GOD.<br /> <br /> I have run a Vampire game where one of the players reaches Golconda, their own state of enlightenment. I have played a game where characters Ascend. If you ask me, it's these games that really explore the true depths of what it means to be what you are either as a Mage or Vampire. And even get a few answers. In the case of the Mage, his story ended when he ascended. In case of the Vampire, he continued to play but was fantastically and fundamentally changed from that point on to the degree that his entire view of reality was altered. His goals shifted. His allies fell away and thought him different. His enemies were afraid of him.<br /> <br /> Games like these give the player the option of exploring very deeply, creating for yourself, what the essence of a Mage or a Vampire really is, and maybe giving you some actual answers to the BIG questions of reality and the universe. Those who say this is a boring, dead-end game likely haven't run one of these games, haven't had a fellow player achieve THEIR characters goal, or they just want their campaign to <i>never end</i>. Well, every story has an end. Where do you want that end to be? Doesn't HAVE to end with Ascension. You could start dealing with higher ideas, higher ideals, and be that METAFORCE that needs to drive people on other realms.<br /> <br /> Really. I am floored by peoples genuine lack of imagination. Sounds like you guys would make terrible storytellers and even WORSE mages in real life.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Vampire game was incredible. The mage that Ascended decided to drop his character because he wanted it to end there. Enlightenment can mean many things. Whatever you want it to mean. If you don't want to play a game where players achieve the <i>ultimate goal</i> <i>of the game that the name implies</i>... <b>Ascension</b>... I think you're intentionally keeping your eyes down and like many Mages, you won't be the ones to ascend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13189-knowledgeseeker","name":"Knowledgeseeker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T10:46:27-07:00","id":1302267,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>The last post in this thread was from 2016. Please don't dig up old posts just to insult people. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T10:52:12-07:00","id":1302269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowledgeseeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964515-ascension?p=1302240#post1302240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something something something Golconda</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel Golconda is fundamentally different in that there are notionally characters who've reached that state and still walk around a la Rebekah and have also fallen out of it (again a la Rebekah). We have no such analog for Mage and it's suggested, much like Wraith transcendence, that your character goes *poof*<br /> <br /> I do feel there's an implied assumption with a number of posts, the OP was &quot;Out of curiosity has anyone ever run a game where their Player Characters actually achieved Ascension?&quot; of &quot;and you kept going&quot;.<br /> <br /> To answer the post at hand, yes but not a playing character. There's a very intimate option for a character to reach Ascension where it's more or less coming to peace with the character's role in the Tapestry. Another option is the apex of the path of occultation where the character removes their fingerprints from reality. That one was emotional as the characters had a long running relationship with someone who they ultimately forgot (Arcane 9!). Such tricks with memory tend to be moving.<br /> <br /> I've also had my characters interface with Oracles and Exemplars which show an utter alien-ness to Ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T08:16:15-07:00","id":1302556,"title":"","content":"<i>Sorry if my previous post came off as harsh.</i><br /> <br /> I'm fascinated by the Ascension concept. The less defined it is, the more mysterious it is. All greater concepts should be less defined if you want to keep the mystery; Antediluvians, Grandmother, Ascension, Oracles, Gods, etc. So the hard part of role playing a game after someone reaches ascension is to make it interesting without defining too much of what happens. That's the thing; Once you NAME something or slap a label of meaning on it, it suddenly BECOMES that, to the exclusion of anything that is NOT THAT. So then you've boxed it in in some manner, giving it definition and meaning. And by doing so, it suddenly means less than it did, or has less potential than it did. Certain groups of Mages are known to do this. Start defining things until they mean something that fits in their world view instead of leaving it Unbound by human comprehension.<br /> <br /> That is the difference between Modern Age and the Mythic Age. One is understood by being quantified, the other is understood intuitively... actually, that's just my interpretation. But I think it's very fitting.<br /> <br /> So to run a fun game where things go beyond Ascension, the POWER of what you are dealing with needs to have meaning. The way to keep that meaning and/or mystery is to not name so much of it, don't quantify it. Keep the explanations loose. Otherwise those powerful beings you now know about (or have joined) seem... somehow less. You don't want that. That ruins the awesomeness when what you have achieved feels mundane like the real world. A Storyteller can easily go wrong in this department and make the Ascension experience feel like another version of our world; Same archetypes, same power struggles, same hierarchies, etc. There IS a reason why these powerful beings are ill-defined. The mystery is what makes them wonderful and the sheer power is hard for people to imagine and cognize, so writers and game lines (myself included) stop describing stuff at some point because there just isn't any <i>real world reference </i>for one's imagination to draw upon. If you're lucky, you can be creative enough and make it work. But, these are not games for everyone just as elder Vampire games and Archmage games are not for everyone.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13189-knowledgeseeker","name":"Knowledgeseeker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T09:01:22-07:00","id":1302574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowledgeseeker</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So <b>to run a fun game where things go beyond Ascension</b>, the POWER of what you are dealing with needs to have meaning. The way to keep that meaning and/or mystery is to not name so much of it, don't quantify it. Keep the explanations loose...<br /> ...Storyteller can easily go wrong in this department and make the Ascension experience feel like another version of our world; Same archetypes, same power struggles, same hierarchies, etc. There IS a reason why these powerful beings are ill-defined. The mystery is what makes them wonderful and the sheer power is hard for people to imagine and cognize, so writers and game lines (myself included) <b>stop describing stuff at some point</b> because there just isn't any <i>real world reference </i>for one's imagination to draw upon</div> </div> </div> </div>Pray tell, how do you, as ST, propose to present a scene w/o describing stuff? How does a character interacts with a scene w/o describing actions? How do you <i>narrate. </i>Do we start speaking in poetry and metaphor or it's the <i>substance </i><i>of the word </i> too much of a burden for the mystery? (most words, after all, tend to mean something)<br /> <br /> Because right now it sounds like you're saying that the least you explain and and name the better...and in that case the best way to narrate Ascencion it's to...not narrate at all. &quot;Close the curtain&quot;, That way you have to name nothing, explain nothing, and you keep the purity of the mistery 100% intact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, these are not games for everyone just as elder Vampire games and Archmage games are not for everyone. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no. Elder Vampires and Archmages may have an alien experience of the world, but you can totally <b>describe </b>what happens to them and WoD does it all the time. They use nouns, verbs and adjectives to describe what they want and what they do. What you're depicting it's a completely different level of &quot;not for everyone&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-04-2019, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T10:18:46-07:00","id":1303349,"title":"","content":"What if ascension is just the beginning?<br /> <br /> In Master of the Arts a prime 10 Archamage can create an universe that is nothing but a mere shadow of the original with their citizens being lower dimensional beings.<br /> <br /> Maybe when a mage ascends he becomes more real gaining a dimension and stopping being a shadow by reaching a higher universe but who says this is the true one? What if reality is just a matrioska of universes and dimensions? and how many times do you have to ascend to become real?<br /> <br /> I like cosmic horror <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T05:23:52-07:00","id":1303501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Master of the Arts a prime 10 Archamage can create an universe that is nothing but a mere shadow of the original with their citizens being lower dimensional beings. </div> </div> </div>Prime 9 can do that.<br /> <br /> Who knows what a Prime 10 Archmage could be able to do?. Perhaps only the Exemplars know, since their goal it's to get there. Perhaps not even they know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T11:33:49-07:00","id":1303807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964515-ascension?p=1303349#post1303349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if ascension is just the beginning?<br /> <br /> In Master of the Arts a prime 10 Archamage can create an universe that is nothing but a mere shadow of the original with their citizens being lower dimensional beings.<br /> <br /> Maybe when a mage ascends he becomes more real gaining a dimension and stopping being a shadow by reaching a higher universe but who says this is the true one? What if reality is just a matrioska of universes and dimensions? and how many times do you have to ascend to become real?<br /> <br /> I like cosmic horror <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This interfaces well with theme of Scion of &quot;there's something bigger beyond&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T12:57:34-07:00","id":1304677,"title":"","content":"I've had some ideas. Let me know what you think of them. Some are mostly rough ideas that have come to me as I daydream. So far the core concept I have to most of these ideas is the realization that your &quot;soul&quot; or &quot;Self&quot; isn't truly within the world that you preside in but is actually resides within the reality in which all souls reside. This allows for the perspectives of the self affirming and self denying sort of mages to be both right and wrong. The self denying folks are right in that they don't have a self but get some good news when they fully realize what they are and the Self affirming folks realize that the soul they thought they have isn't some thing they &quot;have&quot; it's what they ARE. So based off this here are some ideas.<br /> <br /> 1. A Transhumanist setting where humans obtained &quot;geniuses&quot; personal A.I. shells that quantify the self of the individual and slowly help the individual come to enlightenment by having this software shell be an accountant, teacher, friend, guide, therapist, and occasionally a lover (See the movie: Her). Both the Virtual Adepts (Sponsored by the tradition), Trans humanist Independent Mages, and the Technocracy begin developing these shells. Eventually as more people come to accept this technology and become more enlightened that was the moment in which the singularity started to become closer and closer. As technology began to develop faster and faster on a personal level people began realizing this core idea as they were being connected to the global web through B/CI technologies: your soul/self isn't here it's actually elsewhere and we're all right next to each other but appear disparate. Awakening isn't the process of turning on the power switch but a process of remembering bits and pieces (which feel immense) of who, what, when, where, why, and how you are and what you are capable of. More and more people were awakening every year at an exponential rate. Both mystic techniques and technologies also began to develop at an exponential pace due to the rapid onset of the newly awakened and awakened hypertech present in the world. After the singularity there may have a been a few who have ascended but the vast majority are awake but still on earth with a radically transformed earth. Technology is abundant, many social ills have been solved thanks to people being better able to communicate, all energy and matter is reorganized into computronium or other similar wonders that can be installed with intelligent software/minds billions of times smarter than a human in 2019, other flora and fauna seems to have ties to souls and begin to awaken aswell (That's right you can chill and do magick with the tree in your backyard), and trans humanity has a uniting principle to all paradigms, not only that it turns out the Caul doesn't actually invert your soul but makes you think that's what happened and distorts the messages and lessons of your avatar. Your &quot;True Soul&quot; cannot be affected in that matter. The aliens horrors beyond are just the projections of trauma that life has been dealing with while attempting to survive through the terror of evolution of the past. Not really sure what to do with Marauders and other supernaturals in this setting but you guys are creative, I'm sure you can do something. In the end Transhumanity (this includes the awakened flora and fauna) has a pretty cool place to live, the digital web being present as a layered AR and VR landscape, the umbra being explorable to all, a solar system being adapted for all life, and the improvement of the sentient condition. What happens to the factions and what happens between the new millenium and this post singularity existence is up to you.<br /> <br /> However there are still a few questions What are these souls? Is this &quot;well of souls&quot; heaven? the beyond? Nirvana? Brahman? is the pathway within or without? can everyone ascend or is that for a selected few? is there life out there in the Deep Universe? and if so are they connected to this well of souls or do they have their own &quot;well&quot;? do they have Mages? Transhumanity may have the keys to the cosmos but they still have yet to open all the doors. The universe is ripe for exploring and perhaps there are other universes parallel. Will it be like the old days of colonialism as these new explorers venture out into the dangerous deep universe? or will our expeditions resemble the mantra of the federation from Star Trek? Not only that the Umbra is still infinite and expansive and it might be an good idea to see if mages who have left earth are still in the near realms. Not only that how should we deal with them? and do they even want the society and new tools that we have?<br /> <br /> Who knows.<br /> <br /> 2. Once one Ascends they essentially fully realize that they are a transcendent Soul connected to all others throughout and beyond space-time. Think of it as having a set of Virtual reality gear on this whole time and you &quot;awaken&quot; for a second time in the true reality. You didn't achieve ascension you just remember that's what you always are and will ever be eternally. Their family members that have either perished or have not encountered in the material worlds turned out to be right next to you hoping one day you would truly &quot;awaken&quot; and are happy to see you or may be asleep right next to you attempting to find Ascension and you see their soul suffering in their slumber (gotta add some horror in there). From here it's up to you as to the nature of this ascended plane as an ST. Is it what people call Nirvana, Heaven, Asgard etc? and is the center of all realms all universes, omni verses?. How many souls are there and how many of them are in a state of remembrance? and how many are in that state of having that metaphorical virtual reality gear on. What exactly happened did people do this voluntarily or is there something else going on here?<br /> <br /> From here while you still have sphere magick you have completely transcended focus and are beyond what many call &quot;holy, pure, divine etc.&quot;. You have realized what you truly are and it is completely up to the player as to what the true nature of their soul is but it's highly doubtful that you are some kind of malevolent being. You feel a transcendent connected force and feel connected to all existence at all times and you feel as though you are a particle in the water that is God. Your choice is simple, go back to your material projection and guide others as an Oracle while having an infinite essence rather than the meager 4 essences you were taught or stay in the &quot;True Reality&quot; in an attempt to try and guide your companions and family from &quot;afar&quot; and help them reach the state you have gained. The Oracle game would be about mentoring potential candidates for ascension and working with other oracles to help the reality that you came from Ascend, or As an ascended attempt to guide the other players and NPC's in your game indirectly to have them go through their &quot;second awakening&quot;, work on the project of complete and universal ascension, and take inventory on what the fuck just happened how you got trapped in material projections in the first place.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways those are just some ideas. These are just rough ideas that you guys can play with and I am fully aware they aren't perfect. There's probably alot more to flesh out but I hope this proves that it is perhaps possible to play as an Ascended/Oracle and still have some mystery and opportunities for roleplay and an interesting story to tell.. Who knows maybe I'll add more as I think of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5677-nionusus","name":"nionusus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5677_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T05:27:10-07:00","id":1305021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nionusus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/964515-ascension?p=1304677#post1304677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had some ideas. Let me know what you think of them. Some are mostly rough ideas that have come to me as I daydream. So far the core concept I have to most of these ideas is the realization that your &quot;soul&quot; or &quot;Self&quot; isn't truly within the world that you preside in but is actually resides within the reality in which all souls reside. This allows for the perspectives of the self affirming and self denying sort of mages to be both right and wrong. The self denying folks are right in that they don't have a self but get some good news when they fully realize what they are and the Self affirming folks realize that the soul they thought they have isn't some thing they &quot;have&quot; it's what they ARE. So based off this here are some ideas.<br /> ...<br /> Anyways those are just some ideas. These are just rough ideas that you guys can play with and I am fully aware they aren't perfect. There's probably alot more to flesh out but I hope this proves that it is perhaps possible to play as an Ascended/Oracle and still have some mystery and opportunities for roleplay and an interesting story to tell.. Who knows maybe I'll add more as I think of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you've just defined what Ascencion *is*. Clearly and explicitly. Also note that the books don't do that. Note that the books leave Ascencion as a mystery to be defined by the ST. Once it's defined, yeah, it's playable (altrough current rules don't apply anymore).<br /> <br /> Now that we can use words and understand the goals it's <i>playable</i>. It's also not compatible with most Paradigms, as most would be WRONG (In particular Science has all the Answers it's the right one in the 1\u00ba even if there's &quot;magick&quot;, because gods and stuff get explained away as Belief Power. Neither of them it's very friendly for those that believe reality it's ruled by a pantheon or another, nor to those that believes reality it's doomed. Both are very anthropocentric and *nice*).<br /> <br /> Also: you're a enligthened being with no frailties and no antagonists that lives in perfect-land? Not a very fun play if you can't lose. I would rather go with Awakening version where you want to travel to the superior world to join the fight against the Exarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-15-2019, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}